{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The basic vue app example to get started with the TanStack vue-store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"App.vue"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport Increment from './Increment.vue';\nimport Display from './Display.vue';\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n  <p>Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends like cats or dogs</p>\n  <Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n  <Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n  <Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n  <Display animal=\"cats\" />\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"store.js"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createStore } from '@tanstack/vue-store';\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Vue components too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\nexport function updateState(animal) {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Display.vue"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/vue-store';\nimport { store } from './store';\n\nconst props = defineProps({ animal: String });\nconst count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[props.animal]);\n</script>\n\n<!-- This will only re-render when `state[props.animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render -->\n<template>\n  <div>{{ animal }}: {{ count }}</div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStore"},{"type":"text","value":" remains available as a deprecated alias to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Increment.vue"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { store, updateState } from './store';\n\nconst props = defineProps({ animal: String });\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button @click=\"updateState(animal)\">My Friend Likes {{ animal }}</button>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe basic vue app example to get started with the TanStack vue-store.\n\n**App.vue**\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport Increment from './Increment.vue';\nimport Display from './Display.vue';\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n  <p>Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends like cats or dogs</p>\n  <Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n  <Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n  <Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n  <Display animal=\"cats\" />\n</template>\n```\n\n**store.js**\n```js\nimport { createStore } from '@tanstack/vue-store';\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Vue components too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\nexport function updateState(animal) {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**Display.vue**\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/vue-store';\nimport { store } from './store';\n\nconst props = defineProps({ animal: String });\nconst count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[props.animal]);\n</script>\n\n<!-- This will only re-render when `state[props.animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render -->\n<template>\n  <div>{{ animal }}: {{ count }}</div>\n</template>\n```\n\n`useStore` remains available as a deprecated alias to `useSelector`.\n\n**Increment.vue**\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { store, updateState } from './store';\n\nconst props = defineProps({ animal: String });\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button @click=\"updateState(animal)\">My Friend Likes {{ animal }}</button>\n</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\nid: quick-start\n---\n\nThe basic vue app example to get started with the TanStack vue-store.\n\n**App.vue**\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport Increment from './Increment.vue';\nimport Display from './Display.vue';\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <h1>How many of your friends like cats or dogs?</h1>\n  <p>Press one of the buttons to add a counter of how many of your friends like cats or dogs</p>\n  <Increment animal=\"dogs\" />\n  <Display animal=\"dogs\" />\n  <Increment animal=\"cats\" />\n  <Display animal=\"cats\" />\n</template>\n```\n\n**store.js**\n```js\nimport { createStore } from '@tanstack/vue-store';\n\n// You can instantiate the store outside of Vue components too!\nexport const store = createStore({\n  dogs: 0,\n  cats: 0,\n});\n\nexport function updateState(animal) {\n  store.setState((state) => {\n    return {\n      ...state,\n      [animal]: state[animal] + 1,\n    };\n  });\n}\n```\n\n**Display.vue**\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useSelector } from '@tanstack/vue-store';\nimport { store } from './store';\n\nconst props = defineProps({ animal: String });\nconst count = useSelector(store, (state) => state[props.animal]);\n</script>\n\n<!-- This will only re-render when `state[props.animal]` changes. If an unrelated store property changes, it won't re-render -->\n<template>\n  <div>{{ animal }}: {{ count }}</div>\n</template>\n```\n\n`useStore` remains available as a deprecated alias to `useSelector`.\n\n**Increment.vue**\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { store, updateState } from './store';\n\nconst props = defineProps({ animal: String });\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <button @click=\"updateState(animal)\">My Friend Likes {{ animal }}</button>\n</template>\n```\n"}
